---
import styles from "./sections.module.css";
---

<section
  class:list={[
    "about-section short-version",
    styles["about-section"],
    styles["short-version"],
  ]}
  aria-labelledby="short-title"
>
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">The short version</p>
    <h2 id="short-title">How I ended up here</h2>
  </div>
  <div class:list={["short-version-copy", styles["short-version-copy"]]}>
    <p>
      I am a full-stack engineer with a backend bias. Most of the problems I
      enjoy live around APIs, services, cloud infrastructure, authentication,
      and product features that have to survive real production use.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am particularly interested in the points where those things meet. A
      feature is not really finished if deploying it is fragile, debugging it is
      miserable, or the next engineer has to reverse-engineer why it works.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
